0 Right-Angle Drive
0 Name: right-angle.ldr
0 Author: erik-larsen
0 // Two 12 tooth double bevel gears meshing at a right angle, one on a horizontal axle and one
0 // on a vertical axle. The axles cross at x = -60, y = -38, z = 0, and each gear's middle is
0 // 20 LDU from there, where the tips of their bevel cones meet.

0 // Step 1: a Technic plate with holes, and a 1x2 brick with a Technic 1x2 brick on top,
0 // turned so its hole runs along x
1 71 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3738.dat
1 14 -20 -24 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3004.dat
1 14 -20 -48 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3700.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 2: a 4L axle through the Technic brick, and a 2L axle standing in the plate's end hole
1 0 -50 -38 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3705.dat
1 0 -60 -10 0 0 -1 0 1 0 0 0 0 1 3704.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 3: the gears
1 72 -80 -38 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 32270.dat
1 72 -60 -18 0 1 0 0 0 0 1 0 -1 0 32270.dat
0 STEP
